/T (At the national level, the Society of Women Engineers \(SWE\) acts as a not-for-profit educational and service organization with the mission of promoting women in engineering and technology. Our Cornell section strives to emulate the values set forth by nationals, creating a diverse and inclusive community that encourages academic, leadership, professional, and personal excellence. We provide many opportunities throughout the year for our members and other students from the Cornell Engineering community to develop as engineers, professionals, and people of character.)
